Q: Three States CheckBox in AngularJs A: <p>To make a checkbox show an indeterminate state, use the <code>ng-prop-indeterminate</code> directive to set the <code>indeterminate</code> property of the element.</p>
<h1>The DEMO</h1>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;script src="//unpkg.com/angular/angular.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;body ng-app&gt;
    &lt;input type="checkbox"
           ng-model="checkState"
           ng-prop-indeterminate="triState"&gt;
    The Check Box&lt;br&gt;
    &lt;hr&gt;
    &lt;input type="checkbox" ng-model="checkState"&gt;CheckState={{checkState}}&lt;br&gt;
    &lt;input type="checkbox" ng-model="triState"&gt;TriState={{triState}}&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
<p>For more information, see</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://docs.angularjs.org/api/ng/directive/ngProp" rel="nofollow noreferrer">AngularJS ng-prop Directive API Reference</a></li>
<li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Element/Input/checkbox" rel="nofollow noreferrer">MDN HTML Element Reference - input type=&quot;checkbox&quot;</a></li>
</ul>

